 - `Schedule.week(therapist, monday)` returns a therapist's non-cancelled appointments for the week as a dict keyed by each date (all seven days, empty lists included), sorted by start time.
 - New client register in `clients.py`: `Client` dataclass and `ClientBook` with `add(client)` and `find_by_phone(phone)`. Phone numbers are normalized, so `079 123 45 67`, `+41 79 123 45 67` and `0041791234567` all find the same client. Adding a phone number that is already registered raises `ValueError`.
 - `ClientBook.search(text)` returns clients whose name contains `text`, ignoring case, in the order they were added; a blank query returns `[]`.
+- New `reminders.reminder_text(appointment)` returns the text of the reminder SMS: client name, therapist, date, start time and length.
 
 ## 0.1.0
 
diff --git a/src/slotwise/reminders.py b/src/slotwise/reminders.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e052264
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/slotwise/reminders.py
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+"""Reminder texts sent to clients ahead of an appointment."""
+
+from .model import Appointment
+
+
+def reminder_text(appointment: Appointment) -> str:
+    """Return the text of the reminder SMS for `appointment`."""
+    return (
+        f"Hello {appointment.client}, this is a reminder of your physiotherapy appointment "
+        f"with {appointment.therapist.title()} on {appointment.start:%A %d %B} "
+        f"at {appointment.start:%H:%M} ({appointment.minutes} minutes)."
+    )
